From 13eb835894cb8019c0c355ec391ae3831034e555 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:29:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): bot relay pins one route per connection, not
 one per profile [daveey]

The hermes-bots relay pinned (retainProfileSocket), roster-synced and
drained every profile route of every connection. The gateway relay doors
read one install root whichever profile serves them (_relay_root maps
profiles/<p> to <root>), so the extra routes did no work, but each
pin held a remote `hermes serve --isolated` backend's WebSocket open for
the Desktop's lifetime. web_server_idle_exit never saw zero clients, and
the mini carried 9 per-profile backends (~4.8 GB top MEM) whenever the
MacBook Desktop was connected, holding the bb gate on memory pressure.

relayRepresentativeRoutes() now keeps one route per connection (its
default profile, else the first listed). Delivery still dials the exact
target profile on demand, so its socket closes at refcount 0 and the
backend idle-exits.

Tests: relay.test.ts covers the many-profile connection (one pin, one
roster.sync, one drain, on default), the no-default fallback, and
drain-via-default with delivery on the exact target. Three existing
assertions that encoded the per-profile premise were updated. A new
gateway test pins that the doors share one root across profile backends.
